IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P2-section-2-gate`

-- P2-art-14: Article 14 (human oversight) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. The Omnibus did not change Article 14.
-- Every function takes the date asked, the AI system and the harmonisation facts and answers through the gate of P2-section-2-gate.l4: NOTHING when Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 do not apply to the system on the date asked,
-- JUST FALSE where Article 2(2) cuts the Article off, NOTHING where Article 2(13) says it may be limited. Reading a result: JUST TRUE the requirement is met; JUST FALSE the text says no; NOTHING not covered.
-- Paragraph 5 is encoded three ways: the provider's measures (first subparagraph), whether the requirement applies at all (the second subparagraph's exemption: JUST FALSE where it is lifted), and the bar on the deployer, as a decision function and as a prohibition (SHANT) whose breach path is traced.
-- Seam found (not in the plan): paragraph 5 reaches "high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III" (remote biometric identification systems); Annex III is outside my ranges, so whether the system is one of them is a plain yes or no.

§ `Article 14(1): effective oversight by natural persons`

-- src:350 | 1. High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed in such a way, including with appropriate human-machine interface tools, that they can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which they are in use.
@ref Art 14(1) (src:350)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which it is in use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed with appropriate human-machine interface tools` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(1) the high-risk AI system is designed and developed so that it can be effectively overseen by natural persons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 14, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which it is in use` AND `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed with appropriate human-machine interface tools`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed in such a way, including with appropriate human-machine interface tools, that they can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which they are in use"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 14(2): the aim of human oversight`

-- src:351 | 2. Human oversight shall aim to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights that may emerge when a high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, in particular where such risks persist despite the application of other requirements set out in this Section.
@ref Art 14(2) (src:351)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `human oversight aims to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights that may emerge when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, in particular where such risks persist despite the application of other requirements set out in this Section` IS A BOOLEAN
