        JUST (`human oversight aims to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights that may emerge when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, in particular where such risks persist despite the application of other requirements set out in this Section`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Human oversight shall aim to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 14(3): the oversight measures`

-- src:352 | 3. The oversight measures shall be commensurate with the risks, level of autonomy and context of use of the high-risk AI system, and shall be ensured through either one or both of the following types of measures:
-- src:353 | (a) measures identified and built, when technically feasible, into the high-risk AI system by the provider before it is placed on the market or put into service;
-- src:354 | (b) measures identified by the provider before placing the high-risk AI system on the market or putting it into service and that are appropriate to be implemented by the deployer.
@ref Art 14(3) (src:352-354)
-- "either one or both": an alternative, not a conjunction.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the oversight measures are commensurate with the risks, level of autonomy and context of use of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `measures identified and, when technically feasible, built into the high-risk AI system by the provider before it is placed on the market or put into service ensure the oversight` IS A BOOLEAN
      `measures identified by the provider before placing the high-risk AI system on the market or putting it into service, and that are appropriate to be implemented by the deployer, ensure the oversight` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(3) the oversight measures are commensurate with the risks and ensured through one or both types of measures` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 14, "", 3)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the oversight measures are commensurate with the risks, level of autonomy and context of use of the high-risk AI system` AND (`measures identified and, when technically feasible, built into the high-risk AI system by the provider before it is placed on the market or put into service ensure the oversight` OR `measures identified by the provider before placing the high-risk AI system on the market or putting it into service, and that are appropriate to be implemented by the deployer, ensure the oversight`))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The oversight measures shall be commensurate with the risks ... and shall be ensured through either one or both of the following types of measures"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 14(4): what the natural persons are enabled to do`

-- src:355 | 4. For the purpose of implementing paragraphs 1, 2 and 3, the high-risk AI system shall be provided to the deployer in such a way that natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate:
-- src:356 | (a) to properly understand the relevant capacities and limitations of the high-risk AI system and be able to duly monitor its operation, including in view of detecting and addressing anomalies, dysfunctions and unexpected performance;
-- src:357 | (b) to remain aware of the possible tendency of automatically relying or over-relying on the output produced by a high-risk AI system (automation bias), in particular for high-risk AI systems used to provide information or recommendations for decisions to be taken by natural persons;
-- src:358 | (c) to correctly interpret the high-risk AI system’s output, taking into account, for example, the interpretation tools and methods available;
-- src:359 | (d) to decide, in any particular situation, not to use the high-risk AI system or to otherwise disregard, override or reverse the output of the high-risk AI system;
-- src:360 | (e) to intervene in the operation of the high-risk AI system or interrupt the system through a ‘stop’ button or a similar procedure that allows the system to come to a halt in a safe state.
@ref Art 14(4) (src:355-360)
-- The chapeau ("For the purpose of implementing paragraphs 1, 2 and 3") gives the purpose; "as appropriate and proportionate" is folded into each limb's yes or no (fork F-qualifier-fold).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is provided to the deployer in such a way that the natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to do the things listed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to properly understand the relevant capacities and limitations of the high-risk AI system and to duly monitor its operation, including in view of detecting and addressing anomalies, dysfunctions and unexpected performance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to remain aware of the possible tendency of automatically relying or over-relying on the output produced by the high-risk AI system (automation bias)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to correctly interpret the output of the high-risk AI system, taking into account, for example, the interpretation tools and methods available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to decide, in any particular situation, not to use the high-risk AI system or to otherwise disregard, override or reverse its output` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to intervene in the operation of the high-risk AI system or interrupt it through a 'stop' button or a similar procedure that allows the system to come to a halt in a safe state` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(4) the high-risk AI system is provided to the deployer so that the natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled to do the following` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 14, "", 4)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the high-risk AI system is provided to the deployer in such a way that the natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to do the things listed` AND `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to properly understand the relevant capacities and limitations of the high-risk AI system and to duly monitor its operation, including in view of detecting and addressing anomalies, dysfunctions and unexpected performance` AND `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to remain aware of the possible tendency of automatically relying or over-relying on the output produced by the high-risk AI system (automation bias)` AND `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to correctly interpret the output of the high-risk AI system, taking into account, for example, the interpretation tools and methods available` AND `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to decide, in any particular situation, not to use the high-risk AI system or to otherwise disregard, override or reverse its output` AND `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to intervene in the operation of the high-risk AI system or interrupt it through a 'stop' button or a similar procedure that allows the system to come to a halt in a safe state`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the high-risk AI system shall be provided to the deployer in such a way that natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate:"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 14(5): systems referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III`

-- src:361 | 5. For high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III, the measures referred to in paragraph 3 of this Article shall be such as to ensure that, in addition, no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority.
@ref Art 14(5) first subparagraph (src:361)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures referred to in paragraph 3 are such as to ensure that, in addition, no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(5) first subparagraph the measures ensure that no action or decision is taken unless the identification is separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 14, "", 5)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III": the paragraph reaches those systems and no others (seam: Annex III point 1(a))
        ELSE JUST (`the measures referred to in paragraph 3 are such as to ensure that, in addition, no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the measures referred to in paragraph 3 of this Article shall be such as to ensure that, in addition, no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:362 | The requirement for a separate verification by at least two natural persons shall not apply to high-risk AI systems used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum, where Union or national law considers the application of this requirement to be disproportionate.
@ref Art 14(5) second subparagraph (src:362)
-- JUST TRUE the requirement applies; JUST FALSE the text lifts it (both limbs of the exemption are needed: the use, and the law's view that the requirement is disproportionate). Only the first subparagraph's systems are in point (scope NOTHING otherwise).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Union or national law considers the application of the requirement for a separate verification to be disproportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(5) second subparagraph the requirement for a separate verification by at least two natural persons applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 14, "", 5)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III": the paragraph reaches those systems and no others (seam: Annex III point 1(a))
        ELSE JUST (NOT (`the high-risk AI system is used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum` AND `Union or national law considers the application of the requirement for a separate verification to be disproportionate`))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirement for a separate verification by at least two natural persons shall not apply to high-risk AI systems used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum, where Union or national law considers the application of this requirement to be disproportionate"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:361 | 5. For high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III, the measures referred to in paragraph 3 of this Article shall be such as to ensure that, in addition, no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority.
-- src:362 | The requirement for a separate verification by at least two natural persons shall not apply to high-risk AI systems used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum, where Union or national law considers the application of this requirement to be disproportionate.
@ref Art 14(5) (src:361-362)
-- JUST TRUE the deployer is barred (the requirement applies and the identification has not been so verified and confirmed); JUST FALSE it is not barred (the "unless" is satisfied, or the exemption lifts the requirement).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Union or national law considers the application of the requirement for a separate verification to be disproportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(5) the deployer is barred from taking an action or decision on the basis of the identification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 14, "", 5)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III": the paragraph reaches those systems and no others (seam: Annex III point 1(a))
        ELSE JUST ((NOT (`the high-risk AI system is used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum` AND `Union or national law considers the application of the requirement for a separate verification to be disproportionate`)) AND (NOT `the identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority`))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons ... The requirement ... shall not apply"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Regulative rule of Article 14(5)`

DECLARE `Art 14(5) deployer act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 14(5) take an action or decision on the basis of the identification resulting from the system`

-- src:361 | no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority.
-- src:362 | The requirement for a separate verification by at least two natural persons shall not apply to high-risk AI systems used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum, where Union or national law considers the application of this requirement to be disproportionate.
@ref Art 14(5) (src:361-362)
-- "no action or decision is taken by the deployer ... unless ...": a prohibition on the deployer, with no time limit. The act breaches it (BREACH); with no act the rule stays open (RESIDUAL). The "unless" and the exemption turn the prohibition off (FULFILLED: nothing is prohibited).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Union or national law considers the application of the requirement for a separate verification to be disproportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 14(5) deployer act`
`Art 14(5) the deployer's prohibition on acting on an identification that is not separately verified` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 14, "", 5)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF `the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III` AND (NOT (`the high-risk AI system is used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum` AND `Union or national law considers the application of the requirement for a separate verification to be disproportionate`)) AND (NOT `the identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority`)
        THEN PARTY Deployer
             SHANT `Art 14(5) take an action or decision on the basis of the identification resulting from the system`
             HENCE FULFILLED
        ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the condition of the text is not met
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the Section does not apply on the date asked, or Article 2(2) cuts it off, or Article 2(13) says it may be limited
